<p>In the latest development in the US-Israel conflict with Iran, President Donald Trump said US and Israeli strikes have “knocked out” much of Iran’s military capability. He also argued the US joined the fighting because he believed Iran was about to attack first. His comments came as his administration faced scrutiny over how it explains the decision to enter the war—and what, exactly, the end goal is. Several reports describe shifting and sometimes conflicting public explanations from senior US officials. Secretary of State Marco Rubio initially suggested the US struck after learning Israel was about to take military action, and that Iran would respond by targeting US forces—then later walked back any implication that Israel “forced” Washington’s hand.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/CETy8s3XBBooHCZlpIArB_I6YLTntudobn2P08a2Mq4acmMakqv4D4xfLp18YlekbSvrWlrax4BsIIu71SDTX-6kQxWkJ80o1aTmOvOZX2KuqMmQZ9oIK_oF9vkLnZrwI6e-wVLhDCItUmfDxpHeOWGNDB8NBScwTyy-E_qVwHILgYkCO-T8TDc1o7Ffy-sM0XeMGCvp_JFSX9hp3uzmJUWZJosqrzB-g1ZsgX8N41QGyMhQTGsWgFiGKPs_clQUCIce7v0Lq6kJHHXibQ' alt='President Donald Trump speaks amid scrutiny over the rationale for US strikes on Iran.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Backlash management: The Guardian said Trump’s insistence that Israel did not “force” US action was meant, in part, to tamp down a growing anti-Israel backlash in Congress and within his own political coalition.</li><li>Oval Office setting: Trump gave his assessment during an Oval Office press conference with visiting German Chancellor Friedrich Merz.</li><li>Claimed defections: Trump said some members of Iran’s surviving leadership want to “lay down arms” and seek immunity, though Iran has not publicly indicated it is ready to do so.</li><li>Damage claims: Trump said the campaign had “knocked out” Iran’s navy, air force, radar, and air-detection systems.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Donald Trump: Trump said he ordered US forces to join the fighting because he believed Iran was about to strike first. He also rejected the suggestion that Israel forced the US to act. (<a href='https://time.com/7382322/trump-iran-war-progress-knocked-out-reason-for-strikes/'>TIME</a>)</li><li>Secretary of State Marco Rubio: Rubio initially framed the decision around advance knowledge of imminent Israeli action and concern that Iran would then target US forces. He later walked back any implication that Israel compelled US strikes. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/03/world/middleeast/israel-iran-strikes-rubio.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Democratic lawmakers: Democrats criticized the administration’s briefings and stressed that Congress holds the power to declare war. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/mar/03/trump-israel-iran-war'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Israeli government (as described): A New York Times investigative account said Netanyahu was determined to end diplomatic negotiations, a move that helped push Trump toward military action. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/middleeast/100000010747206/how-trump-decided-to-go-to-war.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Commentators and MAGA supporters (as described): Al Jazeera said Rubio’s remarks fueled debate across the political spectrum, including within Trump’s MAGA base, as the public rationale for the strikes shifted. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/4/rubio-claim-of-israeli-role-in-us-iran-attack-reverberates-despite-denial'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/03/03/trump-says-everythings-been-knocked-out-in-iran-but-offers-no-clear-plan-for-war'>Trump says &#x27;everything&#x27;s been knocked out&#x27; in Iran but offers no clear plan for war</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/us-israel-iran-war-donald-trump-marco-rubio-offer-conflicting-reasons-for-us-entry-into-iran-war-11166545#publisher=newsstand'>Trump, Rubio Offer Conflicting Reasons For US Entry Into Iran War</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/middleeast/100000010747206/how-trump-decided-to-go-to-war.html'>How Trump Decided to Go to War</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://novaramedia.com/2026/03/03/us-bombed-iran-because-israel-was-going-to-attack-anyway/'>US Bombed Iran Because Israel Was Going to Attack Anyway</a> - novaramedia.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/4/rubio-claim-of-israeli-role-in-us-iran-attack-reverberates-despite-denial'>Rubio claim of Israeli role in US Iran attack reverberates, despite denial</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/trump-insists-he-struck-iran-his-own-terms'>Trump insists he struck Iran on his own terms</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/mar/03/trump-israel-iran-war'>Trump denies that Israel forced US’s hand in launching strikes against Iran</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://time.com/7382322/trump-iran-war-progress-knocked-out-reason-for-strikes/'>Trump Says Iran Has Been ‘Knocked Out,’ Denies Israel Forced U.S.’ Hand on Strikes</a> - time.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/update-3-trump-rubio-offer-conflicting-reasons-for-us-entry-into-iran-war'>Trump, Rubio offer conflicting reasons for US entry into Iran war</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://dw.com/de/news-kompakt-usa-begr%25C3%25BCnden-iran-angriff-mit-israel-pl%25C3%25A4nen-s%25C3%25BCdsudan-frankreich-atomwaffen-merz-trump/a-76192273'>U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio discloses that the initial U.S. attack on Iran was due to an Israeli intention to attack Iranian leadership, which would have jeopardized U.S. forces in the region.</a> - dw.com</li></ul>